From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xorbidden <xorbidden@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:27:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] framebuffer: let a panel driver use two framebuffers; fix
 tearing

A device whose own driver feeds the panel (the Mi 9T's command-mode
DSI panel) registers a struct hakios_panel with start, second_buffer,
first_buffer and show. Frames are then drawn into the buffer not on
screen and shown when complete (fb_flip=0 keeps one buffer).
GenericARMPE starts the panel just before the framebuffer. Without a
registered panel nothing changes.

Two more tearing causes, fixed for every device: a swap's surfaces stay
"in use" (MiniIOSurfaceDisplayUse) until copied, and SwapEnd/SwapWait
return only after the copy. CoreAnimation had drawn into one surface
in five while it was being copied.

The new fb_flip argument is added to the boot-argument catalogue and
common_defconfig.

Tested on the Mi 9T: no tearing, SpringBoard at 60 Hz.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
